# STRESS 09 — OVERFLOW AND THE DIAGNOSTICS
#
# THIS SHEET DOES NOT BUILD WITHOUT --allow-overflow. That is the point.
#
#   treekillbot build examples/stress/09-overflow.pulp -o 09.pdf --allow-overflow
#
# Overflow is an ERROR by default (DESIGN.md D9): a dense form that does not
# fit is a document bug, and the most useful thing the tool can do is name the
# box, the height it needed and the height it had. `--allow-overflow`
# downgrades every one of them to a warning; CI does not use it.
#
# The sheet prints the warnings it expects to provoke. Build it and compare
# stderr against the list — if the tool says less than the sheet claims, the
# tool has gone quiet about something.

page
  size: letter
  margin: 0.5in

defaults
  font: IBM Plex Sans
  font-size: 8pt
  color: gray(0.12)

section
  height: 28pt
  text "09 · OVERFLOW AND THE DIAGNOSTICS"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 14pt
    font-weight: bold
    tracking: 1.2pt

section
  height: 20pt
  text "Six diagnostics, in this order — they are sorted by source position — each prefixed with file:line:column in gcc format so an editor parses them for free:"
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 132pt
  padding-top: 4pt
  border-left-width: 2pt
  border-color: gray(0.6)
  padding-left: 9pt
  text "warning: W030 `line-height` sets text leading, not the spacing of ruled lines"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt
  text "warning: W010 content does not fit in this section  (needs 120pt, has 82pt, short by 38pt)"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt
  text "warning: W020 text was shrunk to 8.25pt to fit"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt
  text "warning: W020 text was shrunk to 8.50pt to fit"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt
  text "warning: W021 text does not fit and was clipped"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt
  text "and once for the whole build, not tied to a line:"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)
    padding-top: 3pt
  text "warning: some characters are not in any embedded font and were dropped: 'Α' (U+0391), 'Β' (U+0392), 'Γ' (U+0393), 'Δ' (U+0394), 'α' (U+03B1), 'β' (U+03B2), 'γ' (U+03B3), 'δ' (U+03B4)"
    font: IBM Plex Mono
    font-size: 6.5pt

section
  height: 26pt
  valign: bottom
  text "The exit code matters as much as the text. 3 is a source error, 4 is warnings under --strict, 1 is the tool itself failing. A build tool's callers ask exactly one question: is my input wrong, or is the tool broken?"
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 66pt
  padding-top: 4pt
  gap: 16pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "without --allow-overflow"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      text-transform: upper
      tracking: 0.6pt
    text "E010 on every box that does not fit; nothing is written; exit 3."
      font-size: 7.5pt
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "with --allow-overflow"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      text-transform: upper
      tracking: 0.6pt
    text "W010 instead; the PDF is written and the content really does spill; exit 0."
      font-size: 7.5pt
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "with --allow-overflow --strict"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      text-transform: upper
      tracking: 0.6pt
    text "The same warnings, the PDF is still written, and exit 4."
      font-size: 7.5pt
      padding-top: 3pt

# `width` outside a row. It used to be ignored on everything except a column,
# and a section got W031 for the trouble. It is honoured everywhere now, so this
# band is 200pt wide and there is no warning to show.
section
  height: 24pt
  width: 200pt
  border-width: 0.4pt
  border-color: gray(0.6)
  valign: bottom
  text "`width: 200pt` — honoured, no warning"
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.3)

# W030 — the line-height / line-pitch trap. Both names are real, so a document
# that sets the wrong one gets the default pitch and no error at all.
section
  height: 56pt
  padding-top: 6pt
  box
    height: 46pt
    border-width: 0.4pt
    border-color: gray(0.6)
    line-style: ruled
    line-height: 2.5
    line-color: gray(0.82)

# W010 — an 82pt band asked to hold 120pt of fixed-height children. Under
# --allow-overflow the third box really does hang past the bottom edge, into
# the empty band left below it for exactly that purpose.
section
  height: 90pt
  padding-top: 8pt
  box
    height: 40pt
    border-width: 0.4pt
    border-color: gray(0.5)
    valign: middle
    padding-left: 6pt
    text "40pt"
      font-size: 7pt
  box
    height: 40pt
    border-width: 0.4pt
    border-color: gray(0.5)
    valign: middle
    padding-left: 6pt
    text "40pt"
      font-size: 7pt
  box
    height: 40pt
    border-width: 0.4pt
    border-color: gray(0.5)
    valign: middle
    padding-left: 6pt
    text "40pt — this one hangs out of the band"
      font-size: 7pt

section
  height: 44pt

section
  height: 92pt
  padding-top: 12pt
  gap: 14pt

  # W020 — auto-shrink lets a run step down in quarter-points to a 6pt floor.
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 66pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "W020 — auto-shrink: 0.6 lets this run step down in quarter-point increments until it fits, to a floor of 6pt. It started at 11pt and the warning names the size it landed on, so you can decide whether that size is acceptable or whether the box should simply be bigger."
        font-size: 11pt
        height: 50pt
        auto-shrink: 0.6

  # W021 — shrinking is allowed but only down to 0.95 of the size, which is
  # not enough, so the tail is clipped and the warning says so. W021 is only
  # reachable WITH auto-shrink: with it off, WrapText returns the unclipped
  # layout and text overruns its box in silence.
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 66pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.6)
      padding: 5pt
      text "W021 — auto-shrink: 0.95 is not enough room to manoeuvre, so this run is clipped instead and the warning names both the height available and the height the text needed. Several lines are lost off the bottom of the box, and the box itself is not redrawn: the text simply stops."
        font-size: 9pt
        height: 50pt
        auto-shrink: 0.95

section
  height: 34pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Missing glyphs are the quiet one: gopdf substitutes a space, so a dropped character leaves a hole rather than a box. The line below is Greek set in IBM Plex Mono, which has no Greek."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 30pt
  padding-top: 6pt
  column
    width: 200pt
    text "ΑΒΓΔ αβγδ in Mono:"
      font: IBM Plex Mono
      font-size: 9pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "ΑΒΓΔ αβγδ in Sans:"
      font: IBM Plex Sans
      font-size: 9pt

section
  height: fill
  valign: bottom
  text "Decorations never overflow: they floor their counts, so a ruled box that is one pitch too short simply draws one rule fewer. Only boxes and text can overflow, and only text can shrink."
    font-size: 6.5pt
    color: gray(0.5)
